<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Buildmax half yr shr rises, no dividend.</title>
<headline>Buildmax half yr shr rises, no dividend.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pro-forma results for half year ended Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     11.2	  vs 6.8</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   2.43	  vs 1.43</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   3.26	  vs 1.63</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.84	  vs 0.20</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.40	  vs 0.47</p>
<p>    Turnover		  48.19	 vs 38.28</p>
<p>Full name: Buildmax Ltd (building and construction)</p>
<p>NOTE - Results are pro-forma as the building products group was listed on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange in July 1996.</p>
<p>Directors said the group's year-end would be changed to June 30 to be in line with new controlling shareholder Malaysia's Mycom Berhad. The first set of audited results will therefore cover a period of 15 months to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>It is company policy to pay a single dividend. It will be declared in August 1997 and paid in September, they said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
